**Definition 2.1 (mode cuts and native records).** For each authentic
predecessor $P$ and $\mu\in\{0,1\}$, take the existing gate1 route and
separate HistoryMode input $\mu$. Let $h(P,\mu)$ be its cut immediately
after that actual IN6 and before EX70. Put

$$
\mathcal H_{\mathrm{mode}}
=\{h(P,\mu):P\text{ is an authentic predecessor},\ \mu\in\{0,1\}\}.
$$

A native row record here is a mathematical projection of that actual
row and successor: physical active-code regime, actual row/PC and routine
phase with bank-parity variant, actual post-row latch4 and latch6, and any
actual OUT release. These are not PC numerals stored inside a simulated
bank state. TMC PR57.03 supplies the public native PC/routine meaning;
ARC Definition 2.2 identifies public helper latch4 and ingress latch6.
This notation does not install an experiment or add any coordinate to
$Q$. Its original-response projection is a separate condition in §5.

